Phase 9: Final Project Demonstration
For the actual project demo, you can demonstrate it in this order:
Demo 1 — Login
Show the student login page and successfully log in.
Demo 2 — Dashboard
Show the available learning features.
Demo 3 — AI Question Answering
Enter:
"Explain object-oriented programming with a real-life example."
Show Gemini's generated response.
Demo 4 — Follow-up Question
Ask:
"What are the four main principles?"
This demonstrates conversational context.
Demo 5 — Quiz Generation
Enter:
"Generate 5 multiple-choice questions about Python."
Display the generated quiz.
Demo 6 — Summarization
Upload/paste study material and request:
"Summarize this into important exam points."
Demo 7 — Learning History
Show previously asked questions and generated learning content.
Demo 8 — Error Handling
Demonstrate what happens when:
•	No question is entered.
•	The API is unavailable.
•	Invalid input is submitted.
•	The user is not authenticated.
